# Warnings that the cleanup and stage phases may print (extended regular
# expressions, one per line). Any other warning fails the run, because a
# warning means that the server was not changed as declared.

# RDS and Cloud SQL do not let the admin read pg_authid.
^warning: cannot read the password verifiers of existing roles?
^warning: --target is in effect

# Known limitation, plain PostgreSQL 16+ (the local target): the server
# grants every role a non-superuser creates to its creator, and --prune
# keeps roles granted to the connected user, so they stay between runs.
^warning: (role|user) "e2e_[a-z_]+" is granted to the connected user "[^"]+"; not pruned$

# Known limitation, RDS and Cloud SQL: the admin is not a member of the
# roles it creates, so dbfence predicts that REASSIGN OWNED fails on
# --prune. The roles own nothing, and the services let the admin drop
# them, so the prune succeeds anyway.
^warning: role "e2e_[a-z_]+": "[^"]+" does not have its privileges, so dropping it with --prune will fail at REASSIGN OWNED; run GRANT "e2e_[a-z_]+" TO "[^"]+" first$
